        <section class="pg-band pg-band--paper">
            <div class="pg-wrap">
        <!-- Five Controls -->
        <div class="text-center">
            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary">Five Controls. One Body of Evidence.</h2>
            <p class="text-secondary fw-medium mb-0">Each control closes a specific, common path to a breach. VeriState reporting then shows you, and anyone who asks, that each one is working.</p>
        </div>
        <ControlCards />
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="pg-band pg-band--paper">
            <div class="pg-wrap">
        <!-- Four Outcomes -->
        <div class="mb-5">
            <div class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary">Four Outcomes, One Deterministic Control Set</h2>
                <p class="text-secondary fw-medium">Every engagement is scoped against these four liabilities, not just against threats</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row g-4">
                <!-- Insurance-Grade Protection -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="h4 fw-bold text-primary mb-1">Company Risk</span>
                        <span class="h6 fw-medium text-secondary mb-2">Insurance-Grade Protection</span>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Cyber insurance applications commonly require organisations to confirm that controls such as MFA, endpoint protection and protected backups are in place. We independently verify those controls, maintain evidence of their operation and help your organisation provide accurate information to its broker or insurer. This supports more informed underwriting and reduces the risk of a gap between what was declared and what was operating at the time of an incident.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- Director Defensibility -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-1">Personal Risk</span>
                        <span class="h6 fw-medium text-secondary mb-2">Director Defensibility</span>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Section 180 exposure is personal, and it survives whatever coverage the company carries. We align your control environment to SMB1001 Level 3 (Gold) and exceed it in the areas examined first under forensic review so individual directors have an independently verifiable standard of care to point to.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- Operational Continuity -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-1">Business Risk</span>
                        <span class="h6 fw-medium text-secondary mb-2">Operational Continuity</span>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Prevention will eventually fail once; containment cannot be allowed to fail alongside it. 
                            We architect around minimal blast radius, so a single compromised credential or device is a contained incident, not a firm-wide outage or a notifiable data breach.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- Proof of Care -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-1">Evidentiary Risk</span>
                        <span class="h6 fw-medium text-secondary mb-2">Proof of Care</span>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            A control that cannot be evidenced at a specific point in time is, forensically and legally, indistinguishable from a control that did not exist. We issue timestamped, cryptographically signed reports on control status, on a regular cadence a contemporaneous record your insurer, regulator, or counsel can rely on without taking your word for it.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
            </div>
        </section>
        <CallToAction />
    </div>
    <BriefingForm hidden={true} />
      <!-- Dynamic Modals Rendered from Dataset -->
  {allControls.map((control) => (
    <ControlModal control={control} />
  ))}
</BaseLayout>
